{
  "changelog": "Initial release \u2014 export spatiotemporal data to KML/CZML for virtual globes.\n\n- Supports export to KML (with TimeStamp, ExtendedData, and popup info) and CZML (with time intervals), usable in Google Earth and Cesium.\n- Includes synthetic mode to generate sample flight track data with timestamps for demo purposes.\n- Accepts input from GeoJSON, CSV, and local raster/vector files.\n- Outputs KML, CZML, JSON, and optional GeoTIFF (track density raster); each run produces a manifest.\n- Runs locally and offline by default; synthetic mode requires no network and ensures privacy.\n- Provided with MIT license.",
